  = help: write a date, as in `x: date("2020-03-01")`

== no_axis_to_place_by
error[Z0401]: `annotate` writes at a place on the `y` axis, but nothing is mapped to `y` yet
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:17
  |
4 | d.plot(x: dose).annotate(text: "here", x: 2, y: 1)
  |                 ^^^^^^^^ needs a `y` axis
  |
  = help: map a variable to `y` where the plot starts, or add the layer that maps it before the annotation

== a_size_of_zero
error[Z0401]: `size:` of `annotate` is the size of the type in points of 1/72 inch, above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:44
  |
4 | p.annotate(text: "here", x: 2, y: 1, size: 0)
  |                                            ^ not a size
  |
  = help: write a size such as 8 or 10; without `size:` the text is 8 points, as the labels of the axes are

== zero_on_a_log_scale
error[Z0401]: `y` has 1 value at or below 0, which has no place on a log scale: row 1 of annotation
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:16
  |
4 | p.scale_y(log).annotate(text: "here", x: 2, y: 0)
  |                ^^^^^^^^ the `y` axis is a log scale
  |
  = help: keep the rows with a value above 0, as in `where(y > 0)`; a square-root scale, `sqrt`, holds 0

== a_text_that_is_a_number
error[Z0401]: `text` of `annotate` must be a Str, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:18
  |
4 | p.annotate(text: 3, x: 2, y: 1)
  |                  ^ an Int
  |
  = help: usage: `p.annotate(text: Str, x: Float | Str | Date | DateTime, y: Float | Str | Date | DateTime, size: Float)`

